description:
/crates/kith-store/src/message.rs:71-108 (insert method), line 86

Pattern: advance_state_counter() called BEFORE INSERT, returned value stamped in state_version.
Invariant: state_version = counter at insertion/update time; used by get_changes_since() to track deltas.

Risk: update_delivery_state() and update_read_at() correctly call advance_state_counter() first,
but there's no enforced pattern. If a new method is added later (e.g., update_thread_id),
developer might forget to advance counter first, breaking get_changes_since() semantics.

Solution: Add mandatory doc comment to Message struct or insert() method:
  /// INVARIANT: state_version is set by INSERT/UPDATE methods BEFORE the row is written.
  /// advance_state_counter() is called first, and its returned value is stamped on
  /// state_version. This ensures every message change is tracked by get_changes_since().
  /// When adding new update methods: call advance_state_counter(), then UPDATE with
  /// SET state_version = ?N.

Impact: Reduces accidental logic bugs in message state tracking.
